## Key Learnings

* BENIGN traffic contains heavy tails and burst spikes → robust baselines (median/IQR + quantiles) are mandatory
* Multi-file drift validates SOC reality: “normal” behavior is not static and shifts by day/activity
* Rate-based telemetry features are powerful but risky: they create false positives during benign bursts
* Baselining is the foundation for detection engineering; models without baselines create noisy alert systems

